      "title": "高齡受刑人在監生活狀況與出監轉銜機制之質性研究",
      "title_en": "A Qualitative Study on the Living Conditions and Release Transition Mechanisms of Elderly Prisoners in Taiwan",
      "abstract": "高齡受刑人的在監處遇與出監轉銜是當前矯正實務亟待關注的議題。截至2025年3月，全台矯正機關收容60歲以上高齡受刑人達2,693名，其多元處遇需求已超出以往矯正機關所能因應的範疇。本研究採質性研究取向，針對北、中、南、東四區矯正機關承辦出監轉銜業務之7名第一線矯正工作者進行半結構式深度訪談，以主題分析法歸納四大主題，探究高齡受刑人的在監保護性處遇與出監轉銜機制現況。\n\n研究發現，高齡受刑人類型多元，矯正機關已逐步推動多元保護性處遇，涵蓋體適能、懷舊課程、宗教教化及微型創業訓練，並透過混齡共融模式安排年輕受刑人協助日常生活，硬體設施亦逐步改善。出監轉銜機制上，各機關透過調查表單、場舍主管通報及跨科室合作等多項管道篩選個案，以資料核實與實地訪談兩條路徑進行評估。然而轉銜困境涉及刑期變動頻繁、戶籍異地、社福身份中斷及跨機關協力資源落差等困境，現行更生保護機制偏向短期協助，難以滿足高齡受刑人回到社會的長期生活支持需求。\n\n本研究建議強化矯正機關跨部門協作、建立個別化轉銜評估機制，並將高齡受刑人納入長期照顧政策體系，以落實高齡友善之社會安全網，並期滿足社會保安需求。",
      "abstract_en": "The in-prison treatment and release transition of elderly prisoners represent pressing concerns in contemporary correctional practice. As of March 2025, Taiwan's correctional institutions housed 2,693 prisoners aged 60 and above, whose diverse care needs have increasingly exceeded the capacity of traditional prison management. This study adopts a qualitative research approach, conducting semi-structured in-depth interviews with seven frontline correctional staff responsible for release transition services across four regions—Northern, Central, Southern, and Eastern Taiwan. Using thematic analysis, four major themes were identified to examine the current state of protective treatment and release transition mechanisms for elderly prisoners.\n\nThe findings reveal that elderly prisoners are a heterogeneous population, and correctional institutions have progressively implemented diversified protective treatment measures, including fitness activities, reminiscence programs, religious counseling, and micro-entrepreneurship training. An age-integrated living model, in which younger inmates assist elderly peers with daily routines, has also been adopted, and physical facilities have been gradually improved. Regarding release transition mechanisms, institutions identify cases through multiple channels—survey forms, ward supervisor referrals, and interdepartmental collaboration—and conduct assessments via dual pathways of document verification and in-person interviews. However, significant barriers impede smooth transitions, including frequent sentence modifications, residence registration issues in different jurisdictions, interruption of welfare eligibility, and resource discrepancies across agencies. Current aftercare protection measures tend toward short-term assistance and are insufficient to meet the long-term living support needs of elderly ex-prisoners.\n\nThis study recommends strengthening cross-departmental collaboration within correctional institutions, developing age-differentiated transition assessment tools, and integrating elderly prisoners into the long-term care policy framework in order to build an age-friendly social safety net.",
      "keywords": "高齡受刑人、出監轉銜、保護性處遇、社會復歸、社會安全網",
      "keywords_en": "Elderly Prisoners; Release Transition; Protective Treatment; Social Reintegration; Social Safety Net",
      "display_presenters": "李莉娟",
      "author_info_lines": [
        "李莉娟",
        "南臺科技大學財經法律研究所｜助理教授"
      ]
