      "title": "單一腰部穿戴式三軸加速度感測器之活動監測與久坐提醒系統開發",
      "title_en": "Preliminary Validation of an Activity Monitoring and Sedentary Reminder System for Middle-Aged and Older Adults Using a Single Waist-Worn Triaxial Accelerometer",
      "abstract": "隨著高齡化社會發展，如何透過穿戴式科技協助日常活動監測與久坐管理，已成為智慧健康照護的重要研究方向。本研究開發一套基於單一腰部穿戴式三軸加速度感測器之活動監測與久坐提醒系統，旨在建立低成本且具即時監測能力之活動辨識原型平台。系統以 WiFiBoy 蒐集腰部三軸加速度訊號，首先透過個人化坐姿與站姿雙基準校正建立使用者姿態基準，再利用兩階段規則式判別方法辨識坐姿、站姿及行走三種活動狀態。辨識結果透過 Wi-Fi 與 MQTT 傳送至 Node-RED 平台，進行活動狀態即時顯示、活動時間累計、連續久坐時間計算及久坐提醒。為評估系統之活動辨識可行性，本研究招募 5 名受試者，於受控室內環境進行坐姿、站姿與行走等活動測試，共分析 75 個活動試次及 7,078 個資料視窗，整體 Accuracy 為 95.14%，Macro F1-score 為 95.19%。另進行即時系統功能測試，共取得 2,259 筆有效三分類紀錄，Accuracy 為 95.17%，Macro F1-score 為 94.51%。結果顯示，本系統在受控室內環境下可維持穩定之三分類活動辨識表現，並可完成活動監測、資料傳輸、活動時間紀錄及連續久坐提醒等功能。未來可進一步擴大受試者人數，納入高齡者及不同日常生活情境，以評估系統於居家健康促進與高齡照護應用之可行性。",
      "abstract_en": "With the development of an aging society, the use of wearable technologies to support daily activity monitoring and sedentary behavior management has become an important research direction in smart healthcare. This study developed an activity monitoring and sedentary behavior reminder system based on a single waist-worn three-axis accelerometer, aiming to establish a low-cost activity recognition prototype platform with real-time monitoring capabilities. The system uses WiFiBoy to acquire three-axis acceleration signals from the waist. Personalized dual-baseline calibration for sitting and standing postures is first performed to establish the user’s postural reference, followed by a two-stage rule-based classification method to identify three activity states: sitting, standing, and walking. The recognized activity states are transmitted via Wi-Fi and the MQTT protocol to a Node-RED platform for real-time activity display, activity duration accumulation, continuous sedentary time calculation, and sedentary behavior reminders. To evaluate the feasibility of activity recognition, five participants were recruited to perform sitting, standing, and walking activities in a controlled indoor environment. A total of 75 activity trials and 7,078 data windows were analyzed, yielding an overall accuracy of 95.14% and a Macro F1-score of 95.19%. In addition, a real-time system functional test was conducted, resulting in 2,259 valid three-class records, with an accuracy of 95.17% and a Macro F1-score of 94.51%. The results demonstrated that the proposed system maintained stable three-class activity recognition performance in a controlled indoor environment and successfully integrated activity monitoring, data transmission, activity duration recording, and continuous sedentary behavior reminders. Future studies should recruit a larger number of participants, including older adults, and evaluate the system under diverse activities of daily living to further assess its feasibility for home-based health promotion and elderly care applications.",
      "keywords": "穿戴式感測器、三軸加速度感測、活動辨識、久坐提醒、智慧健康照護",
      "keywords_en": "Wearable Sensor, Three-Axis Accelerometer, Activity Recognition, Sedentary Behavior Reminder, Smart Healthcare",
      "display_presenters": "莊采穎",
