      "title": "中高齡者轉入非典型就業推拉機制與心理調適之質性研究",
      "title_en": "A Qualitative Study on the Push-Pull Mechanism and Psychological Adjustment of Middle-aged and Elderly Workers Transitioning into Atypical Employment",
      "abstract": "在高齡化與數位平台擴張的雙重趨勢下，中高齡者轉入非典型就業已成為臺灣勞動市場的重要現象。本文以四位45至65歲中高齡工作者為訪談對象，透過半結構式深度訪談，探討其由全時正職轉向外送、鐘點教學與清潔派案等非典型工作的動機與心理調適歷程。研究發現如下：第一，轉職並非單一「經濟被迫」邏輯，而是結構推力（高壓工時、職場摩擦、疫情衝擊）與生活拉力（時間自主、家庭照顧需求）共同作用；第二，受訪者普遍經歷社會比較壓力與身分落差，但多透過「勞動尊嚴」與「務實收入評估」重建自我價值；第三，體力負荷與保障不足構成中高齡非典型工作者的核心風險，彈性雖帶來短期可調適性，卻難以替代長期制度安全；第四，數位工具適應並非絕對障礙，關鍵在於是否有可近性的學習支持與操作友善環境。本文據此提出政策建議：建置跨平台勞動保障機制、擴充中高齡友善職務再設計至非典型場域、建立分眾化數位培力與轉職支持方案，以回應超高齡社會下中高齡勞動參與的多元需求。",
      "abstract_en": "Driven by the dual trends of an aging population and the expansion of digital platforms, the transition of middle-aged and elderly adults into atypical employment has become a significant phenomenon in Taiwan's labor market. Utilizing semi-structured in-depth interviews with four workers aged 45 to 65, this study explores their motivations and psychological adjustment processes as they transition from full-time regular jobs to atypical work, such as food delivery, hourly tutoring, and on-demand cleaning services.\n\nThe findings are as follows:\n\nFirst, career transitions are not driven solely by a logic of \"economic coercion\" but by a combination of structural push factors (high-pressure working hours, workplace friction, and the impact of the pandemic) and lifestyle pull factors (time autonomy and family care needs).\n\nSecond, while interviewees commonly experienced social comparison pressure and identity gaps, most reconstructed their self-worth through \"labor dignity\" and a \"pragmatic assessment of income.\"\n\nThird, physical toll and inadequate protections constitute the core risks for middle-aged and older atypical workers; although flexibility offers short-term adaptability, it cannot replace long-term institutional security.\n\nFourth, adaptation to digital tools is not an absolute barrier; the key lies in the availability of accessible learning support and user-friendly environments.\n\nBased on these findings, this paper proposes policy recommendations: establishing cross-platform labor protection mechanisms, expanding middle-aged and elderly-friendly job redesigns to atypical sectors, and building targeted digital empowerment and career transition support programs to address the diverse needs of middle-aged and elderly labor participation in a super-aged society.",
      "keywords": "中高齡者、非典型就業、平台勞動、心理調適、勞動政策",
      "keywords_en": "Middle-aged and Elderly Adults, Atypical Employment, Platform Labor, Psychological Adjustment, Labor Policy",
      "display_presenters": "陳志羿",
      "author_info_lines": [
        "陳志羿／國立臺灣師範大學工業教育學系技職教育數位碩士在職專班／研究生"
      ]
