      "title": "針對老年人肌少症，結合物理儀器治療和運動治療的最佳方案：一項隨機對照試驗的網絡薈萃分析",
      "title_en": "The optimal regimen combining physical modality and exercise therapy for sarcopenia in elder adults: a network meta-analysis of randomized controlled trials",
      "abstract": "【研究背景與動機】老年人面臨較高的肌少症風險，肌少症會對老年人的肌肉量、肌力和活動能力造成不利影響。多種物理儀器療法，例如全身振動和神經肌肉電刺激，已被證實能夠強化運動訓練對肌少症指標的療效。然而，在不同類型物理儀器治療和運動模式（例如阻力訓練、有氧訓練、複合運動）的結合方案中，尚未確定最佳治療方案用以增加肌肉量、增強力量和恢復功能。\n\n【研究目的】本研究旨在（1）比較結合各種物理治療和運動療法的複合方案之效果；（2）確定肌少症指標的最佳治療方案；（3）確定調節治療效果的潛在因子。\n\n【研究方法】我們有系統地檢索了電子資料庫，檢索範圍從建庫至2024年7月。納入的研究包括觀察物理治療合併運動訓練對肌少症療效之隨機對照試驗。採用frequentist網絡薈萃分析對納入的試驗進行分析。我們估算了肌肉量、腿部力量和簡易體能評估量表（SPPB）的標準均數差（standard mean difference, SMD）及其95%信賴區間（confidence interval, CI）。此外，我們也進行了統合迴歸分析，以探討治療效果的潛在調節因子，結果以β值及其95%可信區間（credible interval, CrI）表示。\n\n【研究結果】最終納入了23篇隨機對照試驗（共421位患者）進行分析，並且確定12種治療方案，其中，神經肌肉電刺激聯合阻力訓練在增加肌肉量（SMD = 0.84；95% CI：0.42，1.26）、抬腿力量（SMD = 1.21；95% CI：0.74，1.68）和SPPB量表（SMD = 0.92; 95% CI: 0.63, 1.21）方面效果最佳。此外，參與者的年齡和訓練量分別是影響肌肉量（ꞵ = –1.76; 95% CrI: –2.48, –0.91）和抬腿力量（ꞵ = 0.76; 95% CrI: 0.24, 1.75）治療效果的顯著調節因子。\n\n【研究結論】本研究結果表明，神經肌肉電刺激能夠為進行阻力訓練的老年人提供最佳的身體活動能力，以對抗肌少症。然而，其治療效果可能會受到患者年齡和訓練量的影響。\n\n【關鍵詞】肌少症、身體活動能力、運動訓練、肌肉量 The optimal regimen combining physical modality and exercise therapy for sarcopenia in elder adults: a network meta-analysis of randomized controlled trials\n\nChun-De Liao 1,2, Che-Li Lin 3,and Shih-Wei Huang 4 1 International Ph.D. Program in Gerontology and Long-Term Care, College of Nursing, Taipei Medical University 2 Department of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation, Shuang Ho Hospital, Taipei Medical University\n\n3 Department of Orthopedic Surgery, Shuang Ho Hospital, Taipei Medical University 4 Department of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation, Wan Fang Hospital, Taipei Medical University",
      "abstract_en": "【Background】Elder people face high risks of sarcopenia which exerts harmful impacts on muscle mass, strength, and physical mobility in elderly. Numerious physical modalities, such as whole body vibration and neuromuscular electrical stimulation (NMES), have been demonstrated to augment efficacy of exercise training on sarcopenic indices. The optimal treatments for muscle mass gain, strength gain, and function recovery have not yet been identified among the regimens combining different type of physical agent and exercise mode (such as resistance training, aerobic training, multicomponent exercise).\n\n【Objective】This study aimed to (1) compare the effects among different regimens combining variety of physical modalities and exercise therapies; (2) identify the optimal treatment option for sarcopenic indices; and (3) identify potential factors moderating the treatment effects.\n\n【Methods】The electronic databases were systematically searched from inception until July 2024. Randomized controlled trials that reported the effects of physical modality plus exercise for older people were identified. The included trials were analyzed through a frequentist network meta-analysis. Standard mean difference (SMD) with 95% confidence interval (CI) was estimated for muscle mass, leg strength, and short physical performance battery (SPPB). Meta-regression analyses were performed to explore any potential moderators of the treatment efficacy and results were expressed as β with 95% credible interval (CrI).\n\n【Results】We included 23 trials (421 patients) for analyses. Among the 12 identified treatment options, NMES plus resistance exercise yielded the highest probobility in increasing muscle mass (SMD = 0.84; 95% CI: 0.42, 1.26), leg strength (SMD = 1.21; 95% CI: 0.74, 1.68), and SPPB function score (SMD = 0.92; 95% CI: 0.63, 1.21). In addition, Participant’s age and training volume were significant factors moderating the treatment efficacy on muscle mass (ꞵ = –1.76; 95% CrI: –2.48, –0.91) and leg strength (ꞵ = 0.76; 95% CrI: 0.24, 1.75), respectively.\n\n【Conclusions】Our findings suggest NMES yields the optimal physical mobility to counter sarcopenia in older individuals undergoing resistance training. However, the treatment efficacy appears to be moderated by patient’s age and training volume.\n\n【Keywords】sarcopenia, physical modility, exercise, muscle mass",
      "keywords": "",
      "keywords_en": "",
      "display_presenters": "廖峻德",
      "author_info_lines": [
        "廖峻德1,2、林哲立3、黃士瑋2,3",
        "1臺北醫學大學護理學院國際高齡健康暨長期照護博士學位學程 副教授",
        "2臺北醫學大學雙和醫院復健醫學部 物理治療師",
        "3臺北醫學大學雙和醫院骨科醫學部 主治醫師",
        "4臺北醫學大學萬芳醫院復健醫學部 主治醫師"
      ]
