      "title": "超高齡社會下高齡家庭照顧者支持系統之分析與建構—以社會生態模式觀點",
      "title_en": "Analysis and Construction of Support Systems for Older Family Caregivers in a Super-Aged Society: A Social-Ecological Model Perspective",
      "abstract": "背景與目的： 本研究旨在以社會生態模型觀點，探討臺灣高齡家庭照顧者在超高齡社會下所面臨的多重挑戰，並分析其需求，進而建構針對高齡家庭照顧者的社會生態支持策略模式。\n\n研究方法： 本研究採用PRISMA篩選指南，蒐集 2017年至2024年間國內學術期刊中，針對高齡家庭照顧者支持策略之相關文獻，進行綜合分析與比較。同時，以本研究所調整的高齡家庭照顧者社會生態模式，來歸納關鍵支持因子。\n\n研究結果： 國內針對此族群的實證研究數量極少，最終僅納入三篇高度相關之研究。文獻分析發現，高齡照顧者面臨極高的照顧負荷，其特徵為：每日平均照顧時數長、照顧年數久，且自覺健康狀況較差。為因應此多重困境，本研究建議支持策略應聚焦於鄰近資源的社會生態層次，包含：高齡家庭照顧群體單位（Caring Unit）、照顧群體支援層面（Partner Connect）與鄰近資源地圖（Resource Map）。\n\n結論與建議： 高齡家庭照顧者因資源尋求不易加上自身能力衰退，屬於高風險族群。建議可利用 Older Carer Caring Unit-Partner Connect-Resource Map (OCCPR) 模式，提供貼近家戶單位的實質支持。未來可持續應用 OCCPR 社會生態模式，深入探究超高齡社會下的高齡家庭照顧者困境，以強化學界與實務界對高齡家庭照顧議題之重視。",
      "abstract_en": "Background and Purpose: This study aims to explore the multiple challenges faced by older family caregivers in Taiwan's super-aged society from a social-ecological perspective. It analyzes their specific needs to construct a targeted support strategy model for older family caregivers based on the social-ecological framework.\n\nMethods: Utilizing the PRISMA guidelines, this study systematically collected and reviewed literature published in domestic academic journals between 2017 and 2024 concerning support strategies for older family caregivers. A comprehensive literature analysis and comparison were conducted. Subsequently, an adapted social-ecological model for older family caregivers was applied to synthesize and categorize key support factors.\n\nResults: Empirical studies focusing on this specific demographic in Taiwan are remarkably scarce, with only three relevant articles meeting the inclusion criteria. The literature analysis reveals that older caregivers experience severe burdens, characterized by prolonged daily caregiving hours, extended years of caregiving, and poor self-perceived health. To address these complex dilemmas, this study recommends focusing on proximal resources within the social-ecological levels: the older caregiver caring unit (Caring Unit), the caregiving support network (Partner Connect), and the proximal resource map (Resource Map).\n\nConclusion and Suggestions: Older family caregivers constitute a high-risk group due to difficulties in accessing resources and age-related functional decline. This study recommends implementing the Older Carer Caring Unit-Partner Connect-Resource Map (OCCPR) model to provide substantial, household-centered support. Future research should further utilize the OCCPR social-ecological model to deepen the investigation into older family caregivers in super-aged societies, thereby enhancing academic and practical attention to this critical issue.",
      "keywords": "社會生態模型觀點、高齡家庭照顧者、超高齡社會、支持策略",
      "keywords_en": "Social-ecological model, older family caregivers, super-aged society, support strategies",
      "display_presenters": "黃菁萍",
      "author_info_lines": [
        "黃菁萍1, *",
        "1 國立中正大學成人及繼續教育學系 博士生",
        "＊ 通訊作者：黃菁萍",
        "聯絡Email: submerge215@gmail.com"
      ]
