      "title": "生成式 AI 輔助之中高齡數位視覺實踐：以地方文化貼圖設計為個案研究",
      "title_en": "Generative AI-Assisted Digital Visual Practices among Older Adults: A Case Study of Local Cultural Sticker Design",
      "abstract": "在生成式 AI 迅速發展的當代，視覺創作正經歷從「技法操練」轉向「意念建構」與「語義轉譯」的 典範轉移，這為受生理機能變化與技術門檻所限的中高齡族群，打開了跨越電繪門檻、 拓展數位參與的新契機。本研究植根於杜威（John Dewey）經驗美學與維高斯基（Lev Vygotsky）社會文化及鷹架理論，主張數位創作的核心在於日常經驗的轉化與生命敘事 延續；在此脈絡下，生成式 AI\n\n不僅是工具，更是協助中高齡者具象化記憶、轉譯生活經驗並重啟社會對話的認知支撐 與文化中介。\n\n本研究採質性個案研究取向，以屏東縣東港鎮安定社區發展協會 20 位初次接觸 AI 的中高齡社區幹部（50–60 歲）為對象，開展為期六週的「人機共生地方文化轉譯」LINE 貼圖設計課程。教學歷程循序帶領學員走過貼圖概論、在地符號挖掘、色彩與圖文編排 ，直到實際運用 AI 進行圖像生成。研究資料涵蓋課堂學習歷程觀察、半結構化深度訪談與學員創作成果， 並以三角檢證檢視分析，確保研究結果的嚴謹性與可信度。\n\n研究發現，學員能靈活融合東港在地特產（如黑鮪魚）與鄉土俚語意象（如「大豐收 」、「尚青」），在創作中展現出豐沛的文化詮釋力與主體性，同時顯著提升自我效能 感。不過在人機互動與圖像生成過程中，學員也確實面臨視力負擔、精細操作不易，以 及對生成介面邏輯理解等生理與認知層面的挑戰。據此，本研究梳理出包含「大尺寸硬 體配置」、「即時協作鷹架」及「微步進展課程設計」的中高齡 AI\n\n地方文化創作教學支持原則，期盼為樂齡數位創意教育的推廣、文化賦權與終身學習實 踐，提供具溫度的實證參照。",
      "abstract_en": "In the era of rapid advances in generative AI, visual creation is shifting from technical skill execution toward conceptual construction and semantic translation. This shift creates new opportunities for middle-aged\n\nand older adults to overcome technological barriers and expand digital participation. Grounded in John Dewey’s aesthetic theory of experience and Lev Vygotsky’s sociocultural and scaffolding theories, this study views\n\ngenerative AI as a cognitive scaffold and cultural mediator that supports the transformation of everyday experiences and life narratives into visual creations.\n\nAdopting a qualitative case study approach, this study involved 20 community leaders aged 50–60 from the Anding Community Development Association in Donggang Township, Pingtung County, all of whom were first-\n\ntime AI users. A six-week “Human–AI Symbiosis and Local Cultural Translation” course was implemented through LINE sticker design activities, covering local cultural symbols, color and typographic composition, and AI-\n\nassisted image generation. Data were collected through classroom observations, semi-structured interviews, and design artifacts, with triangulation used to enhance research credibility.\n\nThe findings indicate that participants successfully integrated local specialties, such as bluefin tuna, with vernacular expressions such as “bountiful harvest” and “fresh and high-quality,” demonstrating cultural\n\nagency and enhanced self-efficacy. However, participants also encountered visual fatigue, fine-motor difficulties, and challenges in understanding interface logic. Accordingly, three instructional support principles were\n\nidentified: large-screen hardware configurations, just-in-time collaborative scaffolding, and micro-stepped instructional design. These findings provide practical, human-centered references for advancing digital\n\ncreative education, cultural empowerment, and lifelong learning among older adults.",
      "keywords": "生成式人工智慧、中高齡學習者、LINE貼圖設計、杜威美學",
      "keywords_en": "Generative AI, Older Adults, Local Cultural Translation, Scaffolding Theory, Digital Empowerment",
      "display_presenters": "林孟儀",
